### SIS1 Task API — HTTP Client collection
### Open this file in IntelliJ IDEA / WebStorm ("Run" arrow next to each request)
### or in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension.
### Run the app first: mvn spring-boot:run  (dev profile, H2 in-memory DB)
### Requests are meant to be run top to bottom in order — later ones (409, update,
### delete) depend on tasks created by the earlier ones.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/tasks


### 1. Create task A — valid payload -> 201 Created (+ Location header)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare SIS1 report",
  "description": "Write the report covering weeks 1-4 material",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-15"
}


### 2. Create a task with a title that already exists -> 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare SIS1 report",
  "priority": "LOW"
}


### 3. Create task B — a second, distinct task (used later for the update-conflict demo)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Review teammate's PR",
  "description": "Look over the pull request before merge",
  "priority": "MEDIUM",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-05"
}


### 4. Create a task — invalid payload -> 400 Bad Request (unified ApiError, field errors list)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "a",
  "dueDate": "2020-01-01"
}


### 5. Create a task — malformed JSON body -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Broken JSON", "priority": }


### 6. Get all tasks — first page, default page size -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}


### 7. Get all tasks — filtered by status, paginated and sorted -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}?status=NEW&page=0&size=5&sort=dueDate,asc


### 8. Get task by id -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/1


### 9. Get task by non-existent id -> 404 Not Found (unified ApiError)
GET {{baseUrl}}/9999


### 10. Get task by malformed id (not a number) -> 400 Bad Request
GET {{baseUrl}}/abc


### 11. Full update of task A -> 200 OK
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare SIS1 report (final)",
  "description": "Updated description after review",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-20"
}


### 12. Update task B with task A's current title -> 409 Conflict
PUT {{baseUrl}}/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare SIS1 report (final)",
  "priority": "MEDIUM"
}


### 13. Update a non-existent task -> 404 Not Found
PUT {{baseUrl}}/9999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ghost task",
  "priority": "LOW"
}


### 14. Update with invalid data (title too short) -> 400 Bad Request
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "ab"
}


### 15. Partial update — change status only -> 200 OK
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "DONE"
}


### 16. Partial update — invalid enum value -> 400 Bad Request
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "FINISHED"
}


### 17. Delete task A -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/1


### 18. Delete a non-existent task -> 404 Not Found
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/9999
